<title>UK: UK bookstores to expand Internet sales sites -FT.</title>
<headline>UK bookstores to expand Internet sales sites -FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading British booksellers Waterstone's and Dillons each plan to launch Internet sites offering more than one million titles this autumn, the Financial Times reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The report said the two would compete with U.S. online booksellers such as Internet specialist Amazon.com and the giant Barnes &amp; Noble Inc retail operation, raising the threat of a price war.</p>
<p>Waterstone's, part of the W.H. Smith retail chain, plans to expand its existing experimental site to stock 1.4 million titles from its October debut.</p>
<p>Dillons, owned by music company EMI Group Plc, will have at least 1.2 million titles on a site it plans to launch with partners in September.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
